Customers in Illinois have reported a total of 671 internet outages.

## Key Findings
• The high number of outages is linked to scheduled maintenance activities and severe weather conditions, which are common causes of disruptions [1].
• Fiber cuts during maintenance have been identified as a contributing factor to the frequency of outages [1].

## Analysis
The data indicates a systemic issue with internet outages in Illinois, primarily driven by external factors such as maintenance and weather. The frequency of 671 reported outages suggests that these disruptions are a significant concern for customers. The recurring nature of these issues points to potential gaps in the current maintenance protocols and infrastructure resilience against weather-related disruptions.

## Recommendations
• Review and optimize maintenance schedules to minimize customer impact, possibly by increasing communication and transparency about planned outages.
• Enhance infrastructure resilience to withstand severe weather conditions, potentially through investment in more robust materials or technology.
• Investigate and address the root causes of fiber cuts during maintenance to prevent future occurrences.

