2025-12-05 01:33:49.500 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
UrbanLink customers prefer to receive updates about network outages via text messages.

## Key Findings
• Customers frequently express a preference for receiving outage updates through text messages rather than emails [1], [2].
• There is a strong desire for timely and transparent communication regarding the status and resolution timelines of outages [3], [4].
• Customers feel frustrated when they are not informed about outages in advance, especially when these affect their work or daily activities [1], [3].

## Analysis
The data indicates a clear preference among UrbanLink customers for receiving updates via text messages. This preference is likely due to the immediacy and convenience of text messages, which can be accessed quickly and easily on mobile devices. The emphasis on timely and transparent communication suggests that customers value being kept in the loop about service disruptions, which can help mitigate frustration and improve overall satisfaction. The lack of advance notifications about outages is a recurring issue, highlighting a gap in UrbanLink's current communication strategy.

## Recommendations
• Enhance the current communication strategy by prioritizing text message updates for outage notifications and status updates.
• Implement a system for advance notifications of scheduled maintenance to reduce customer frustration.
• Regularly review and improve the transparency and timeliness of communication to align with customer expectations.

