2025-12-05 01:34:22.039 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
The estimated resolution time for internet service outages reported by customers in Texas is generally between one to four hours, with some cases lacking a clear estimated time of arrival (ETA).

## Key Findings
• Texas reported 671 internet service outages [1].
• Resolution times in Texas are often estimated between one to four hours [1].
• Some cases in Texas lack a clear ETA, indicating variability in communication and resolution precision [1].

## Analysis
The data suggests that while the frequency of outages in Texas is significant, the resolution process is less consistent compared to other regions like New York. The variability in estimated resolution times and the absence of clear ETAs in some cases may point to systemic issues in communication or resource allocation for resolving outages. This inconsistency can lead to customer dissatisfaction and may affect the overall perception of service reliability.

## Recommendations
- Improve communication protocols to ensure all customers receive a clear ETA for service restoration.
- Analyze resource allocation and operational processes to reduce resolution time variability.
- Consider implementing a more robust tracking system to provide accurate and timely updates to customers.

