2025-12-05 01:34:22.172 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
HarborWest offers loyalty programs and balance-based waivers as alternatives for customers dissatisfied with maintenance fees.

## Key Findings
• Customers can avoid maintenance fees by maintaining a minimum balance, which varies by account tier, such as $1,500 for the Gold tier [1], [2].
• HarborWest offers a loyalty program that can help reduce fees over time, although it may not completely waive them [3].
• There is a temporary promotion mentioned, but its effectiveness in improving fee waiver acceptance is unclear [1].

## Analysis
The data reveals that HarborWest provides structured alternatives to maintenance fees, primarily through balance requirements and loyalty programs. However, these options may not be perceived as competitive compared to other banks like Chase, which are noted for offering better rewards and lower fees [2], [3]. The lack of clear communication about these alternatives and their criteria contributes to customer dissatisfaction. The temporary promotion mentioned does not seem to have a significant impact on customer satisfaction regarding fee waivers [1].

## Recommendations
- Improve communication about fee waiver criteria and loyalty program benefits to ensure customers are fully informed.
- Consider revising the balance requirements or enhancing the loyalty program to make it more competitive with other banks.
- Evaluate the effectiveness of current promotions and explore new strategies to increase customer satisfaction with fee structures.

