2025-12-05 01:35:37.467 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
The main reasons for customer dissatisfaction with the plus plan are chronic slow internet speeds and frequent connectivity issues.

## Key Findings
• Customers frequently report that the internet speeds they experience are significantly lower than the advertised 100 Mbps, often feeling like they are receiving only 30 to 50 Mbps [1], [2], [3].
• Many customers express frustration over constant buffering and slow loading times, particularly during peak hours [4], [5].
• There is a recurring theme of customers considering switching to competitors due to dissatisfaction with the current service [6], [7].
• Some customers are unclear about the plan limits and feel misled about the service they should be receiving [8], [9].

## Analysis
The data reveals a systemic issue with the plus plan's ability to deliver the promised internet speeds, leading to widespread customer dissatisfaction. The frequent mention of slow speeds and connectivity issues suggests that these problems are not isolated incidents but rather indicative of a broader service delivery problem. The consideration of switching to competitors highlights a potential risk of customer churn if these issues are not addressed. Additionally, the lack of clarity regarding plan limits suggests a need for better communication with customers about what they can realistically expect from their service.

## Recommendations
• Investigate and address the root causes of the slow internet speeds and connectivity issues to improve service delivery.
• Enhance customer communication regarding plan limits and expected service levels to manage expectations better.
• Consider offering incentives or solutions to retain customers who are considering switching to competitors.

