2025-12-05 01:36:57.806 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Customers at Civic Trust express frustration about unexpected fees primarily due to system errors and unclear fee structures.

## Key Findings
• System errors and billing oversights are common causes of unexpected fees, with fees ranging from $25 to $200 being applied incorrectly [1], [2].
• Customers are often unaware of the conditions required to avoid fees, such as maintaining a minimum balance or understanding tier-based fee waivers [3], [4].
• Comparisons with other banks, like Chase, highlight dissatisfaction with Civic Trust's fee structures, as customers perceive other banks to offer clearer and more favorable terms [5], [6].

## Analysis
The data reveals systemic issues within Civic Trust's billing system, leading to erroneous fee charges. These errors not only frustrate customers but also damage trust, as evidenced by customers considering switching to competitors with more transparent fee structures. The lack of clear communication regarding fee conditions further exacerbates customer dissatisfaction, indicating a need for improved customer education and system reliability.

## Recommendations
• Enhance system reliability to prevent billing errors and ensure accurate fee application.
• Improve communication with customers regarding fee structures and conditions to avoid unexpected charges.
• Consider revising fee policies to be more competitive with other banks, potentially reducing customer attrition.

