2025-12-05 01:37:13.829 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Loyalty discounts generally have a more significant impact on customer decisions in hotel bookings compared to seasonal promotions.

## Key Findings
• Loyalty promotions are frequently requested by returning guests, especially those at higher loyalty tiers, as they offer long-term benefits such as room upgrades and exclusive discounts [1], [2], [3].
• Seasonal promotions are popular during peak seasons and are often requested by customers looking for short-term savings, such as summer discounts [4], [5].
• Both types of promotions are competitive with offers from other hotel brands, with loyalty promotions often providing better long-term value [6], [7].
• Customers who book frequently throughout the year tend to benefit more from loyalty promotions, while those planning a single trip may find seasonal promotions more advantageous [8].

## Analysis
The data reveals a clear preference for loyalty promotions among frequent travelers and returning guests, as these promotions offer cumulative benefits that enhance the overall value of repeated stays. Seasonal promotions, while popular during specific times of the year, cater more to customers seeking immediate savings for one-off trips. This suggests that loyalty programs are effective in fostering customer retention and encouraging repeat bookings. The competitive nature of these promotions with other hotel brands indicates a strategic approach to maintaining customer loyalty and market competitiveness.

## Recommendations
- Enhance the visibility and accessibility of loyalty programs to attract more frequent travelers and encourage repeat bookings.
- Consider offering hybrid promotions that combine elements of both loyalty and seasonal discounts to appeal to a broader customer base.
- Monitor the effectiveness of seasonal promotions during peak times to ensure they remain competitive and attractive to potential customers.

