2025-12-05 01:37:49.368 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
The upgrade options for the premium plan show differences in pricing and features between customers in California and Florida.

## Key Findings
• In California, the premium plan typically costs around $100 to $125, offering speeds up to 300 Mbps, with no active promotions [1], [2], [3].
• In Florida, the premium plan is priced at approximately $89 to $200, with speeds up to 1 Gbps, and includes additional perks like no throttling during peak hours [4], [5], [6].
• Customers in both states express concerns about the cost of the premium plan compared to competitors like AT&T and Spectrum [1], [4], [5].

## Analysis
The data reveals a significant difference in the pricing and features of the premium plan between California and Florida. In California, the focus is on providing higher speeds and reliability, but the cost is relatively higher without current promotions. In contrast, Florida offers a more competitive price with additional benefits like no throttling, which may appeal to customers with multiple devices. The consistent mention of competitors suggests that customers are actively comparing options, indicating a competitive market environment.

## Recommendations
Consider introducing promotional offers in California to make the premium plan more attractive. Additionally, emphasize the unique benefits of the premium plan in marketing materials to better compete with other providers like AT&T and Spectrum.

