2025-12-05 01:38:43.371 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Customers of SkyBridge Airlines often prefer vouchers over cash refunds because vouchers can offer additional benefits and are processed more quickly.

## Key Findings
• Vouchers are often preferred because they can be worth more than the cash refund, offering additional benefits like bonus miles or discounts [1].
• Cash refunds are typically slower to process, sometimes taking a few weeks, which can be frustrating for customers [1].
• Vouchers are issued more frequently than cash refunds, especially when specific conditions for cash are not met [2].
• Customers sometimes choose vouchers while waiting for a potential cash refund, although this is rare [3].

## Analysis
The preference for vouchers over cash refunds among SkyBridge Airlines customers seems to be driven by both the added value and the speed of processing. Vouchers often come with additional perks, making them more attractive than the equivalent cash amount. The slow processing time for cash refunds further incentivizes customers to opt for vouchers. This pattern suggests that the airline's policy effectively encourages the use of vouchers, which may be more beneficial for the company in terms of customer retention and future bookings.

## Recommendations
Consider enhancing communication about the benefits of vouchers to further encourage their acceptance. Additionally, improving the processing time for cash refunds could address customer frustration and improve overall satisfaction.

