2025-12-05 01:40:38.635 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Guests perceive the cleanliness standards at Beachfront Suites as inferior compared to other hotels, particularly Marriott and Hilton.

## Key Findings
• Guests frequently compare Beachfront Suites unfavorably to Marriott and Hilton, citing better cleanliness standards at these competitors [1], [2], [3].
• Common cleanliness issues at Beachfront Suites include dirty bathrooms, unclean floors, and stained linens, which are not expected at a hotel of its standing [4], [5], [6].
• Several guests expressed disappointment and considered switching to other hotel brands due to these cleanliness issues [7], [8], [9].

## Analysis
The data reveals a consistent pattern of dissatisfaction with the cleanliness standards at Beachfront Suites, which is often compared unfavorably to competitors like Marriott and Hilton. This suggests a systemic issue with the hotel's cleaning protocols, as multiple guests across different locations have reported similar problems. The frequent comparisons to other hotels indicate that guests have higher expectations for Beachfront Suites, which are not being met. This dissatisfaction is significant enough to affect brand loyalty, with some guests contemplating switching to other hotel chains.

## Recommendations
- Conduct a thorough review and enhancement of the cleaning protocols to meet or exceed industry standards.
- Implement regular training sessions for housekeeping staff to ensure consistent cleanliness across all locations.
- Consider offering compensation or incentives to retain dissatisfied guests and rebuild brand loyalty.
- Monitor guest feedback closely to identify and address cleanliness issues promptly.

