2025-12-05 01:41:23.786 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
CozyInn offers alternatives such as rescheduling and credits for future stays to mitigate cancellation fees.

## Key Findings
• CozyInn allows guests to reschedule their stay to avoid cancellation fees entirely, which involves picking a new date for their stay [1].
• Guests can receive credits for future stays if they choose to cancel instead of rescheduling, which can be applied to their next booking [1].
• Partial fee waivers are sometimes available, particularly for loyalty program members, though the extent of the waiver can vary [2], [3].
• CozyInn's cancellation policy is designed to protect against lost revenue from last-minute cancellations, which can significantly impact occupancy rates [3].

## Analysis
The data reveals that CozyInn is attempting to provide flexible options to mitigate the impact of cancellation fees, such as rescheduling and offering credits. However, the effectiveness of these measures may be limited by the perceived complexity and the strictness of the policy, especially for last-minute cancellations. The availability of partial fee waivers for loyalty members suggests an effort to retain customer loyalty, but the overall perception of high fees compared to competitors remains a challenge.

## Recommendations
Consider simplifying the process for obtaining credits or rescheduling to make it more user-friendly. Additionally, evaluate the possibility of offering more competitive cancellation policies, especially for last-minute cancellations, to align better with industry standards and improve customer satisfaction.

