2025-12-05 01:41:35.023 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Premier Resorts' cancellation fees significantly impact customer decisions and satisfaction, with many customers expressing frustration and considering alternative accommodations.

## Key Findings
• Last-minute cancellation fees are perceived as excessively high, often up to 50% of the booking total, leading to customer dissatisfaction and stress [1], [2].
• Customers frequently compare Premier Resorts' policies unfavorably to competitors like Marriott, which are perceived as more lenient [1], [3].
• Both last-minute and advance cancellation fees contribute to customer frustration, although the level of dissatisfaction is generally similar regardless of the timing of the cancellation [2], [4].
• Customers express a desire for more flexible cancellation policies, especially in cases of unforeseen circumstances [5], [6].

## Analysis
The data reveals a systemic issue with Premier Resorts' cancellation fee structure, particularly the high fees for last-minute cancellations. This policy not only frustrates customers but also drives them to consider competitors with more lenient policies. The dissatisfaction is compounded by the lack of flexibility in handling cancellations due to unforeseen circumstances, which customers find unfair. The consistent feedback across multiple interactions suggests that the current policy may be damaging customer loyalty and satisfaction.

## Recommendations
- Consider revising the cancellation fee structure to be more competitive with industry standards, potentially reducing last-minute fees.
- Implement a more flexible policy for cancellations due to unforeseen circumstances to improve customer satisfaction.
- Enhance communication about the fee structure at the time of booking to manage customer expectations and reduce surprise and frustration.

