2025-12-05 01:44:03.120 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Customers at Premier Resorts Miami Beach have experienced billing errors primarily related to incorrect charges for services not used and issues with loyalty perks not being applied correctly.

## Key Findings
• Customers reported being charged for room service and amenities they did not use [1].
• There were issues with loyalty discounts not being applied correctly, leading to higher bills than expected [2].

## Analysis
The recurring theme of incorrect charges for unused services suggests a potential systemic issue in the billing process at Premier Resorts Miami Beach. This could be due to errors in the billing cycle or miscommunication between departments handling guest services and billing. Additionally, the failure to apply loyalty discounts correctly indicates a need for better integration of loyalty programs with the billing system. These issues can lead to customer dissatisfaction, especially among loyal customers who expect seamless service.

## Recommendations
- Implement a review process for billing statements to catch errors before they reach the customer.
- Enhance the integration between the loyalty program and billing systems to ensure discounts are applied correctly.
- Provide training for staff to better handle and resolve billing discrepancies promptly.

