2025-12-05 01:45:48.081 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Northpeak Financial reassures customers about the safety of their accounts during fraud investigations by providing clear communication, updates, and a zero liability policy.

## Key Findings
• Customers are informed that unauthorized transactions will be blocked immediately, and a new card will be issued [1], [2].
• The bank provides a zero liability policy, ensuring customers are not held responsible for fraudulent charges if confirmed [3].
• Customers receive updates on the investigation process, typically via email, to keep them informed about the status of their claims [4].
• Agents emphasize the importance of customer feedback and strive to improve processes based on it [5].

## Analysis
The data reveals that Northpeak Financial has a structured approach to handling unauthorized transactions, focusing on immediate action and clear communication. The reassurance provided through a zero liability policy and regular updates helps mitigate customer anxiety during the investigation process. However, the time taken for resolution, which can be up to ten business days, may still cause frustration among customers, indicating a potential area for process improvement.

## Recommendations
Consider streamlining the fraud investigation process to reduce resolution time, thereby enhancing customer satisfaction. Additionally, continue to emphasize the zero liability policy and provide frequent updates to maintain customer trust and confidence.

