Customers who completed the pre-qualification process had a higher loan approval rate, with 522 approvals compared to 150 for those who did not.

## Key Findings
• Customers who went through the pre-qualification process had 522 loan approvals [1].
• Customers who did not go through the pre-qualification process had 150 loan approvals [2].

## Analysis
The data indicates a significant difference in loan approval rates between customers who completed the pre-qualification process and those who did not. This suggests that the pre-qualification process may play a crucial role in increasing the likelihood of loan approval. The higher approval rate for pre-qualified customers could be due to better preparation and alignment with the lender's criteria, which the pre-qualification process helps to ensure.

## Recommendations
- Encourage more customers to undergo the pre-qualification process to potentially increase their chances of loan approval.
- Analyze the pre-qualification process to identify specific factors that contribute to higher approval rates and enhance these aspects further.
- Monitor the approval rates continuously to ensure that the pre-qualification process remains effective and beneficial for both the customers and the organization.

