2025-12-05 02:09:23.205 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Premier Resorts' cancellation fees significantly impact customer decisions and satisfaction, with many customers expressing frustration and considering alternative accommodations.

## Key Findings
• Last-minute cancellation fees are perceived as excessively high, often up to 50% of the booking total, leading to customer dissatisfaction and stress [1], [2].
• Customers frequently compare Premier Resorts' policies unfavorably to competitors like Marriott, which are perceived as more lenient [1], [3].
• Both last-minute and advance cancellation fees contribute to customer frustration, although the level of dissatisfaction is generally similar regardless of the timing of the cancellation [2], [4].
• Customers express a desire for more flexible cancellation policies, especially in cases of unforeseen circumstances [5], [6].

## Analysis
The data reveals a systemic issue with Premier Resorts' cancellation fee structure, which is a significant source of customer dissatisfaction. The high fees for last-minute cancellations, in particular, are a major pain point, leading some customers to consider switching to competitors with more lenient policies. This dissatisfaction is compounded by the perception that the fees are not justified, especially when cancellations are due to unforeseen circumstances. The consistent feedback across multiple interactions suggests that the current policy may be damaging customer loyalty and could impact future bookings.

## Recommendations
- Consider revising the cancellation fee structure to be more competitive with industry standards, potentially reducing fees for last-minute cancellations.
- Explore offering more flexible cancellation options or exceptions for unforeseen circumstances to improve customer satisfaction.
- Communicate clearly and transparently about cancellation policies at the time of booking to manage customer expectations and reduce frustration.

