Customers in Illinois are experiencing internet outages 671 times due to scheduled maintenance and 671 times due to severe weather conditions.

## Key Findings
• Scheduled maintenance and severe weather conditions each account for 671 instances of internet outages in Illinois [1], [2].
• The frequency of outages due to these causes suggests a recurring issue that affects a significant number of customers.

## Analysis
The data indicates that both scheduled maintenance and severe weather are equally significant contributors to internet outages in Illinois, each causing 671 outages. This pattern suggests systemic issues in both the planning of maintenance activities and the network's resilience to weather conditions. The high frequency of outages due to these factors points to potential gaps in communication with customers about maintenance schedules and the need for infrastructure improvements to withstand severe weather.

## Recommendations
• Enhance communication strategies to inform customers about scheduled maintenance in advance, potentially reducing frustration and confusion.
• Invest in infrastructure improvements to increase network resilience against severe weather conditions, thereby reducing weather-related outages.
• Consider implementing a more robust monitoring system to quickly identify and address fiber cuts during maintenance activities.

