2025-12-05 02:55:30.697 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Luke received a promotional offer from Spectrum that was $10 less than his current payment, which influenced his decision-making by making him consider switching to save money.

## Key Findings
• Luke was offered a promotional rate by Spectrum that was $10 less than his current payment with StreamWave [1].
• The offer from Spectrum made Luke hesitant to upgrade to StreamWave's premium plan, which was $20 more than his current plan [1].
• Luke expressed a desire to save money, indicating that cost was a significant factor in his decision-making process [1].

## Analysis
The data reveals that promotional offers from competitors like Spectrum can significantly impact customer decision-making, especially when cost savings are involved. Luke's case illustrates how a lower-priced offer can deter customers from upgrading to more expensive plans, even if those plans offer better performance. This suggests that price sensitivity is a critical factor for customers when considering service upgrades or changes.

## Recommendations
To retain customers like Luke, StreamWave should consider offering competitive promotional rates or discounts, especially when customers express cost concerns. Additionally, highlighting the value and benefits of higher-tier plans in comparison to competitors' offers could help justify the price difference and encourage upgrades.

