2025-12-05 03:05:49.585 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Internet service outages in Texas and New York are reported with equal frequency (671 each), but resolution times in Texas are generally longer and less predictable compared to New York.

## Key Findings
• Both Texas and New York reported 671 internet service outages [1], [2].
• In Texas, resolution times are often estimated between one to four hours, with some cases having no clear estimated time of resolution [3], [4], [5].
• In New York, resolution times are typically shorter, ranging from under one hour to two to three hours, with more precise estimates provided [6], [7], [8].

## Analysis
The data indicates that while the frequency of outages is the same in both states, the resolution times in Texas are more variable and less certain. This suggests potential inefficiencies in the outage management process in Texas, possibly due to factors like maintenance scheduling or communication issues. In contrast, New York seems to have a more streamlined process, with quicker and more reliable resolution times. This discrepancy could lead to higher customer dissatisfaction in Texas, as evidenced by customer frustrations over the lack of clear communication and longer wait times [3], [4], [5].

## Recommendations
- **Improve Communication in Texas**: Enhance the communication strategy to provide clearer and more accurate resolution times to customers in Texas.
- **Streamline Maintenance Processes**: Investigate the causes of longer resolution times in Texas and implement process improvements to align with the more efficient practices observed in New York.
- **Monitor Customer Feedback**: Regularly collect and analyze customer feedback to identify ongoing issues and address them proactively.

