2025-12-05 03:06:02.407 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Customers in Illinois have reported a total of 671 internet outages.

## Key Findings
• The high number of outages is linked to scheduled maintenance and severe weather conditions, as previously noted.
• Fiber cuts during maintenance activities have been a recurring issue, contributing to the frequency of outages.

## Analysis
The data indicates a systemic issue with internet outages in Illinois, primarily driven by external factors such as maintenance and weather. The frequency of 671 reported outages suggests that these disruptions are a significant concern for customers. The combination of scheduled maintenance and fiber cuts points to potential areas for operational improvement, particularly in minimizing service interruptions during necessary maintenance activities.

## Recommendations
• Enhance communication with customers regarding scheduled maintenance to manage expectations and reduce frustration.
• Implement more robust preventive measures to protect infrastructure from severe weather impacts.
• Review and improve maintenance protocols to minimize the risk of fiber cuts and other disruptions.

