2025-12-05 03:06:02.810 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Customers prefer to receive updates about network outages via text messages.

## Key Findings
• Customers express a preference for receiving outage updates through text messages rather than email [1].
• There is a strong desire for timely and transparent communication regarding the status and resolution timelines of outages [2], [3].
• Customers feel frustrated when they are not informed about outages in advance, especially when it affects their work or daily activities [1], [3].

## Analysis
The data reveals a clear preference among UrbanLink customers for receiving outage updates via text messages. This preference likely stems from the immediacy and convenience of text notifications, which are more likely to be seen promptly compared to emails. The emphasis on timely and transparent communication suggests that customers value being kept in the loop, which can mitigate frustration during service disruptions. However, there is a notable gap in proactive communication, as customers often report feeling uninformed about outages until they experience them firsthand.

## Recommendations
- Implement a robust text notification system to provide real-time updates on network outages.
- Enhance proactive communication strategies to inform customers about scheduled maintenance and potential disruptions in advance.
- Regularly review and improve the transparency and frequency of outage updates to align with customer expectations.

