2025-12-05 03:06:03.989 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
The estimated resolution time for internet service outages reported by customers in Texas is generally between one to four hours, with some cases lacking a clear estimated time of resolution.

## Key Findings
• Resolution times in Texas are often estimated between one to four hours [1].
• Some cases in Texas have no clear estimated time of resolution, indicating variability and unpredictability in service restoration [2].

## Analysis
The data suggests that while there is a general expectation for resolution within one to four hours, the lack of a clear estimated time in some cases points to potential inefficiencies or communication gaps in the service restoration process. This variability can lead to customer dissatisfaction and may indicate systemic issues in outage management or resource allocation.

## Recommendations
- Improve communication with customers by providing more accurate and consistent estimated resolution times.
- Investigate the causes of variability in resolution times to identify and address any underlying operational inefficiencies.
- Consider implementing a more robust outage management system to enhance predictability and customer satisfaction.

