2025-12-05 03:08:13.190 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Customers of SkyBridge Airlines prefer vouchers over cash refunds primarily because vouchers often offer additional benefits such as bonus miles or discounts.

## Key Findings
• Vouchers can be worth more than the cash refund itself, offering additional benefits like bonus miles or discounts [1].
• Vouchers are issued more quickly than cash refunds, which can take several weeks to process [2].
• Some customers appreciate the flexibility of using vouchers for future travel, especially if they plan to fly again soon [3].

## Analysis
The preference for vouchers over cash refunds among SkyBridge Airlines customers seems to be driven by the added value and convenience that vouchers provide. Vouchers not only offer potential financial benefits through additional perks but also are processed faster than cash refunds, which can be a significant factor for customers needing quick resolutions. However, this preference is not universal, as some customers express frustration when they do not plan to travel soon or need immediate cash. This indicates a potential gap in meeting diverse customer needs, suggesting that while vouchers are beneficial for some, they may not be the best solution for all.

## Recommendations
Consider offering more flexible refund options that cater to different customer needs, such as expedited cash refunds for those who require immediate financial relief. Additionally, clearly communicate the benefits of vouchers to customers to enhance their perceived value.

