2025-12-05 03:08:24.663 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Coastal Wings does not offer compensation for flight delays caused by mechanical issues.

## Key Findings
• Coastal Wings consistently does not provide compensation, such as meal vouchers or hotel stays, for delays due to mechanical issues [1], [2].
• Customers express significant frustration and disappointment with the lack of compensation and communication during these delays [1], [2], [3].
• Comparisons to other airlines, such as Delta and United, highlight customer expectations for compensation that Coastal Wings does not meet [1], [3].

## Analysis
The data reveals a systemic issue with Coastal Wings' policy on handling flight delays caused by mechanical issues. The lack of compensation is a recurring theme, leading to customer dissatisfaction and negative comparisons with competitors. This dissatisfaction is compounded by perceived poor communication during delays, which exacerbates customer frustration. The absence of compensation options, even for premium economy passengers, suggests a gap between customer expectations and the airline's current policies.

## Recommendations
• Consider revising compensation policies to include options like meal vouchers or hotel accommodations for delays caused by mechanical issues.
• Improve communication strategies to keep customers informed and reduce frustration during delays.
• Benchmark against competitors to align compensation offerings with industry standards and customer expectations.

