2025-12-05 03:09:15.619 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Some guests at CozyInn feel dissatisfied with the cancellation fees due to perceived high costs, especially for last-minute cancellations, and comparisons to more favorable policies at other hotel chains.

## Key Findings
• Guests express frustration with high cancellation fees, particularly for last-minute cancellations, which can be as high as 55% of the total booking cost [1], [2].
• There is a perception that CozyInn's cancellation fees are stricter compared to competitors like Hilton, which may offer better deals or more flexible policies [1], [3].
• Some guests feel that the cancellation fees are unfair, especially in cases of emergencies or when they have experienced prior service issues [2], [3].
• The dissatisfaction with cancellation fees is linked to a risk of customer churn, as guests consider switching to other hotel chains [4].

## Analysis
The data reveals a systemic issue with CozyInn's cancellation policy, particularly the high fees associated with last-minute cancellations. This policy is perceived as punitive and not competitive compared to other hotel chains like Hilton. The dissatisfaction is compounded when guests face emergencies or have had previous negative experiences with the hotel. The trend of guests considering switching to competitors indicates a potential risk of losing customers if the policy remains unchanged.

## Recommendations
- Consider revising the cancellation policy to offer more flexibility, especially for last-minute cancellations, to align better with industry standards and competitor offerings.
- Implement a more customer-friendly approach for handling emergencies, possibly waiving fees in such cases to improve customer satisfaction.
- Enhance communication about the benefits of the loyalty program to retain customers who might be considering switching to competitors.

