2025-12-05 03:09:35.918 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Customers are frustrated with the lack of proactive notifications regarding delivery delays because the notifications either lack actionable information or are not sent at all.

## Key Findings
• Notifications often lack actionable information, leaving customers without clear next steps [1].
• Some customers did not receive any notifications about delivery delays, leading to increased frustration [2].
• Misleading notifications have been reported, where the information provided did not accurately reflect the delivery status [3].

## Analysis
The data reveals a systemic issue with the notification system for delivery delays. Customers expect to be informed proactively about any delays, but the current system either fails to send notifications or sends ones that do not provide actionable information. This lack of effective communication exacerbates customer frustration, as they are left without guidance on how to proceed or when to expect their deliveries. The comparison to other companies, like Amazon, which have more effective notification practices, highlights the gap in service expectations.

## Recommendations
• Improve the content of notifications to include actionable steps or estimated delivery times to better manage customer expectations.
• Ensure that notifications are consistently sent out for all delays to prevent customers from being uninformed.
• Review and enhance the notification system to prevent misleading information from being sent to customers.

