2025-12-05 03:09:40.720 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
CozyInn offers alternatives such as rescheduling stays and providing credits for future bookings to mitigate cancellation fees.

## Key Findings
• Guests can avoid cancellation fees by rescheduling their stay to a new date, which waives the fees entirely [1].
• If rescheduling is not possible, guests can receive credits for future stays, which can be applied to their next booking [1].
• Partial fee waivers or reductions are sometimes available, particularly for loyalty program members, though these are limited by policy constraints [2], [3].
• Some guests have successfully negotiated partial fee reductions, such as a 30% waiver, though higher reductions are typically not possible [3].

## Analysis
The data reveals that CozyInn is attempting to provide flexible options to mitigate the impact of cancellation fees, which are a common source of guest dissatisfaction. The ability to reschedule or receive credits offers guests some relief, though the complexity of these options may still leave some guests feeling frustrated. The availability of partial fee waivers for loyalty members suggests a tiered approach to customer service, rewarding frequent guests with more favorable terms. However, the strictness of the policy and the limited scope for negotiation may still leave some guests dissatisfied, especially when compared to more flexible policies at competing hotels.

## Recommendations
Consider simplifying the process for obtaining credits or rescheduling to make it more user-friendly. Additionally, evaluate the potential for more flexible cancellation policies, especially for loyalty program members, to enhance customer satisfaction and competitiveness.

