Agents recommended maintaining good account standing, improving credit scores, and providing additional documentation to enhance customers' chances of obtaining a credit limit increase in the future.

## Key Findings
• Agents advised customers to maintain a good account standing and stay with the bank longer to increase eligibility for future credit limit increases [1].
• Customers were encouraged to submit additional documentation to have their accounts reconsidered for a credit limit increase [2].
• Improving credit scores was highlighted as a critical factor for eligibility in future requests [3].

## Analysis
The recommendations provided by agents focus on long-term strategies for improving creditworthiness, such as maintaining a good account standing and improving credit scores. These suggestions indicate that the bank's decision-making process for credit limit increases heavily relies on the customer's financial behavior and history. The emphasis on submitting additional documentation suggests that the bank is open to reconsidering requests if customers can demonstrate improved financial stability or other relevant changes.

## Recommendations
Consider providing customers with more detailed guidance on how to improve their credit scores and what specific documentation could strengthen their case for a credit limit increase. Additionally, offering educational resources on managing credit utilization and payment timeliness could help customers better position themselves for future requests.

