2025-12-05 03:13:00.647 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
The bank reassures customers about the safety of their accounts during fraud investigations by implementing a zero liability policy, providing timelines for resolution, and maintaining communication throughout the process.

## Key Findings
• The bank has a zero liability policy, ensuring customers are not held responsible for unauthorized charges [1].
• Customers are informed about the timeline for resolution, typically within seven to ten business days, and are kept updated via email [2], [3].
• Temporary blocks on accounts and new card issuances are standard procedures to enhance security during investigations [4].
• Customers are encouraged to reset passwords and verify their identity to prevent further unauthorized access [5].

## Analysis
The bank's approach to reassuring customers involves clear communication and proactive measures to protect accounts. The zero liability policy is a strong reassurance, as it directly addresses customer concerns about financial responsibility. Providing a timeline and regular updates helps manage customer expectations and reduces anxiety during the investigation process. The emphasis on security measures, such as password resets and new card issuances, further demonstrates the bank's commitment to safeguarding customer accounts.

## Recommendations
Consider enhancing the speed of the fraud resolution process to reduce customer frustration. Additionally, providing more detailed information about the investigation process could further reassure customers and improve their experience.

