2025-12-05 03:36:44.212 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
The "loyal20" promo code is used as a recovery or compensation tool primarily in situations involving delivery delays for ShopSquare customers.

## Key Findings
• The "loyal20" promo code is offered to customers experiencing delivery delays as a form of compensation [1].
• Customers express frustration with delivery delays, often due to carrier issues, and the promo code is used to mitigate dissatisfaction [2].
• Agents offer the promo code as part of a compensation package, sometimes alongside partial refunds [1].

## Analysis
The use of the "loyal20" promo code as a recovery tool is a strategic response to delivery delays, which are a common issue for ShopSquare customers. The data suggests that these delays are often attributed to external factors such as carrier issues, particularly with FedEx. By offering the promo code, agents aim to retain customer loyalty and address dissatisfaction. This approach indicates a proactive effort to manage customer expectations and reduce potential churn due to service disruptions.

## Recommendations
- Enhance communication with customers regarding delivery status to preemptively address concerns and reduce the need for compensation.
- Consider evaluating and improving partnerships with carriers to minimize delivery delays.
- Monitor the effectiveness of the "loyal20" promo code in retaining customers and adjust compensation strategies as needed.

