2025-12-05 03:44:37.845 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
The most common causes of flight delays leading to customer stress are weather conditions and mechanical issues, which significantly impact rebooking options.

## Key Findings
• Weather conditions are frequently cited as the primary cause of flight delays, leading to customer frustration and stress, especially when they have urgent commitments [1], [2].
• Mechanical issues are another common cause of delays, often resulting in customer dissatisfaction due to limited compensation options [3], [4].
• Rebooking options are typically limited to same-day or next-day flights, which can be inconvenient for customers with tight schedules [5], [6].
• Customers often express dissatisfaction with the compensation offered, such as meal vouchers or travel credits, which are perceived as inadequate [7], [8].

## Analysis
The data reveals that weather and mechanical issues are systemic causes of flight delays, contributing to significant customer stress, particularly when urgent travel plans are disrupted. The limited rebooking options and perceived inadequacy of compensation exacerbate customer dissatisfaction. This pattern suggests a need for airlines to improve communication and offer more flexible rebooking and compensation options to mitigate stress and enhance customer satisfaction.

## Recommendations
- Consider enhancing communication strategies to keep customers informed about delays and rebooking options promptly.
- Explore offering more flexible rebooking options, such as partnerships with other airlines, to provide customers with more immediate alternatives.
- Evaluate current compensation policies to ensure they meet customer expectations and provide meaningful relief during delays.

