2025-12-05 03:53:38.869 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:116 - ## Summary
Resolution times for double-booking issues at LuxStay Hotels are generally faster than for name mismatch issues.

## Key Findings
• Double-booking issues are typically resolved quickly, often within a few minutes, as they primarily involve canceling duplicate bookings [1], [2].
• Name mismatch issues take longer to resolve, often requiring 30 to 45 minutes due to the need for identity verification and documentation checks [3], [4].
• Customers express frustration with the longer resolution times for name mismatches, which can impact their check-in experience [3], [5].

## Analysis
The data indicates that while double-booking issues are straightforward and resolved quickly, name mismatches present a more complex challenge due to the additional verification steps required. This discrepancy in resolution times can lead to customer dissatisfaction, particularly when they are eager to check in or have other plans. The need for identity verification in name mismatches is a significant factor contributing to the delay, highlighting a potential area for process improvement.

## Recommendations
Consider streamlining the verification process for name mismatches to reduce resolution times. This could involve implementing more efficient identity verification technologies or preemptive checks during the booking process to minimize errors.

