2025-12-05 04:08:11.475 | INFO     | __main__:chat_endpoint:165 - ## Summary
Customers suggest improving transparency regarding fees by providing clearer communication and detailed explanations of fee structures.

## Key Findings
• Customers express frustration over unexpected fees, often feeling caught off guard by charges they did not anticipate [1], [2].
• There is a desire for clearer communication about fee structures, as customers often do not recall seeing details about these fees in their booking confirmations [3].
• Comparisons with other brands suggest that some competitors may offer clearer or more flexible fee policies, which customers find appealing [4], [5].

## Analysis
The data reveals a consistent pattern of customer dissatisfaction stemming from a lack of transparency in fee communication. Customers frequently feel surprised by additional charges, indicating that the current methods of conveying fee information may be insufficient or unclear. This issue appears systemic, as it is mentioned across multiple interactions. Additionally, the comparison with competitors suggests that Civic Trust could be at a disadvantage if customers perceive other brands as more transparent or flexible.

## Recommendations
1. Enhance the clarity of fee-related communications by ensuring that all fees are prominently displayed and explained in booking confirmations and other customer interactions.
2. Consider implementing a more detailed breakdown of potential fees during the booking process to set clearer expectations.
3. Monitor customer feedback to identify specific areas where communication can be improved and adjust policies accordingly to align with industry standards.

