## Analysis
The data reveals a disconnect between customer expectations and actual service delivery regarding loyalty tiers and issue resolution speed. While loyalty programs are designed to prioritize loyal customers, operational challenges such as high call volumes and complex issues can negate these benefits. This inconsistency can lead to customer dissatisfaction, as seen in the repeated inquiries about the effectiveness of loyalty tiers. Additionally, the perception that other brands offer better service to loyal customers suggests a competitive gap that some hotels may need to address to retain their loyal clientele.

