## Analysis
The data reveals a systemic issue with frequent internet outages in Illinois, primarily due to scheduled maintenance and weather-related disruptions. These outages are not only frequent but also impactful, as they disrupt daily activities, especially for those working from home. The recurring nature of these outages is leading to customer dissatisfaction and potential churn, as indicated by multiple customers expressing their intent to switch providers if the situation does not improve. The combination of maintenance and weather-related issues suggests a need for improved infrastructure resilience and better communication with customers regarding outage expectations and resolutions.

