## Analysis
The data reveals a notable trend: customers who skip the pre-qualification process are more likely to have their loans approved. This could indicate that the pre-qualification process might be a barrier or deterrent for potential applicants, or it might suggest that the criteria used in pre-qualification are stricter than those applied in the final approval process. This pattern could point to systemic issues in the pre-qualification criteria or its perceived value by customers. Further investigation into the reasons behind this disparity could help in optimizing the loan approval process and improving customer experience.

