## Analysis
The data reveals a systemic issue with frequent internet outages in Illinois, primarily due to scheduled maintenance and weather-related disruptions. These outages are not only frequent but also impactful, affecting customers' ability to work from home and leading to dissatisfaction. The recurring nature of these outages suggests a need for improved maintenance scheduling and communication with customers to manage expectations better. Additionally, the mention of fiber cuts during maintenance indicates potential areas for operational improvement to minimize service disruptions. The trend of customers considering switching providers highlights a churn risk that needs to be addressed to maintain customer loyalty.

