The data indicates that the frequent internet outages in Illinois are largely systemic, stemming from scheduled maintenance and infrastructure issues like fiber cuts. These outages are not isolated incidents but rather recurring problems, as multiple customers have reported experiencing them several times within a short period. This pattern suggests a need for improved communication and planning around maintenance activities to minimize disruptions. Additionally, the lack of timely notifications to customers about these outages has been a point of frustration, highlighting an area for potential improvement in customer service and communication strategies.

