## Analysis
These patterns reveal a common theme of dissatisfaction and a need for transparency in the loan application process. Customers are not only frustrated by the denial but also seek actionable advice to improve their financial standing. This suggests a potential area for banks to enhance customer experience by providing clearer guidance and support post-denial. Additionally, the interest in alternative offers highlights the competitive nature of the banking industry, where customers are willing to switch providers for better terms. This could indicate a need for banks to improve their retention strategies by offering more competitive rates or personalized financial advice.

